{"name":"Spiced Latte","hex":"#886c57","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spiced","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having spice added, spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of spice"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiced"},{"term":"latte","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drink of coffee made from espresso and steamed milk, generally topped with foam.","A similar drink, where the espresso is replaced with some other flavoring ingredient such as chai, maté or matcha (green tea)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pillar capped by a hemispherical stone capital with the flat side facing up, used as building supports by the ancient Chamorro people and now used as a sign of Chamorro identity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latte"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Spices1.jpg/330px-Spices1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice"},{"title":"Latte","blocks":[{"text":"Latte or caffè latte, also known as caffellatte, caffelatte, or rarely caffè e latte, is a coffee drink of Italian origin made with espresso coffee and steamed milk, traditionally served in a glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg/330px-Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latte"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Indianspicesherbs.jpg/500px-Indianspicesherbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Indianspicesherbs.jpg/1280px-Indianspicesherbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Indianspicesherbs.jpg/500px-Indianspicesherbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A group of Indian herbs and spices in bowls","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndianspicesherbs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Spices_of_Sa%C3%BAde_flea_market%2C_S%C3%A3o_Paulo%2C_Brazil.jpg/500px-Spices_of_Sa%C3%BAde_flea_market%2C_S%C3%A3o_Paulo%2C_Brazil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Spices_of_Sa%C3%BAde_flea_market%2C_S%C3%A3o_Paulo%2C_Brazil.jpg/1280px-Spices_of_Sa%C3%BAde_flea_market%2C_S%C3%A3o_Paulo%2C_Brazil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Spices_of_Sa%C3%BAde_flea_market%2C_S%C3%A3o_Paulo%2C_Brazil.jpg/500px-Spices_of_Sa%C3%BAde_flea_market%2C_S%C3%A3o_Paulo%2C_Brazil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spices of Saúde flea market, São Paulo, Brazil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpices_of_Sa%C3%BAde_flea_market%2C_S%C3%A3o_Paulo%2C_Brazil.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Le_livre_des_merveilles_de_Marco_